(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "extends this session's GTG-proven independent-adversarial-review\n    discipline (re-derive from physics literature before reading code) to\n    the ORIGINAL 6 namespaces (kotoba.sm.complex/tensor/vector-field/spinor/\n    gauge/standard-model, ADR-2607051500), which had never received this\n    intensity of review despite predating and being independent of GTG" "landed 2026-07-09/10: kotoba-lang/standard-model#15 merged as\n    519e5da8daff98692a720538e50506ea8848c50f, 80 tests/2918 assertions\n    (up from 79/2911), CI green JDK17+21; superproject pin advanced via API\n    single-entry commit df6500d3629421e57c5f2741d48def5af1d52b65" "BUG: covariant-derivative-sm built the U(1)_Y gauge generator from raw\n    fermion hypercharge :Y, not :Y/n-2. This namespace's own GMN convention\n    (Q=T3+Y/2, already correctly checked by gell-mann-nishijima-ok?) requires\n    Y/2. After electroweak mixing (via this namespace's own mixing-matrix/\n    photon-Z inverted), photon coupling = e*(T3+Y_eff) since\n    e=g*sin(theta_W)=g'*cos(theta_W) (independently satisfied by this\n    namespace's own mass/mixing functions) -- equals required e*Q=e*(T3+Y/2)\n    only for Y_eff=Y/2. Raw Y gives e*(T3+Y), wrong for every charged\n    fermion with T3!=0 -- 50% too large in magnitude for e_L specifically\n    (T3=-1/2,Y=-1: (T3+Y)/(T3+Y/2)=1.5)" "why undetected at original landing: the only test of\n    covariant-derivative-sm exercised exclusively the fields-off case, where\n    U(1) generator normalization cannot matter. No test decomposed the\n    combined SU(2)/U(1) output into the physical photon direction and\n    checked against e*Q -- classic each-piece-verified-in-isolation gap" "requester independently re-verified before merge: re-derived\n    e*(T3+Y_eff)=e*Q algebra from scratch, and while building an even\n    stronger regression test caught+fixed a coupling-constant argument-order\n    mistake in that test's OWN first draft (passing gw=1.0 instead of g)\n    before it could land a subtly-wrong passing test -- same\n    verify-the-verification discipline applied throughout this session" "fix: (gauge/u1-generators (:Y fermion) dim) ->\n    (gauge/u1-generators (/ (:Y fermion) 2.0) dim). Added\n    covariant-derivative-sm-photon-coupling-matches-e-times-Q: pure-photon\n    field config (Z-component exactly zero), checks e_L coupling against\n    -i*e*Q*psi exactly plus explicit check pre-fix value would be 1.5x too\n    large -- regression strong enough to have caught this at original landing" "no other bugs found: complex/tensor core algebra, spinor's gamma\n    matrices/Dirac equation, gauge's SU(2)/SU(3) generators+structure\n    constants (self-interaction slot-order pattern independently reconfirmed\n    correct for the ORIGINAL compact-group case too), CKM matrix (checked\n    via independent 3-rotation matrix product, matched to floating-point\n    noise), Higgs sector -- all matched independent derivation from physics\n    literature" "coverage gaps noted but NOT fixed (not bugs, thin tests around\n    already-correct code): gell-mann-nishijima-ok? tautological for 18/21\n    fermion-table entries (only 3 independently spot-checked); photon-Z/\n    mixing-matrix only tested for norm preservation (would not catch sign\n    flip or A/Z swap); M_W=M_Z*cos(theta_W) and CKM unitarity tested at only\n    1 fixed point each; covariant-derivative-sm's :color/:weak fermion-map\n    shape never wired to fermion-content's :multiplet shape (part of why the\n    hypercharge bug went unexercised against the real table); yang-mills-density\n    test mislabels its n=0 branch as U(1) (real U(1) always has n=1)" "methodological consequence: THIRD real bug this session's independent-\n    review discipline found in this repo (after PR #6, PR #11), and the\n    first found in code that was NOT freshly-written -- the presumption that\n    older/settled code is comparatively low-risk was wrong. This discipline\n    (re-derive before reading, decompose combined systems and check the\n    combination not just isolated pieces, independently re-verify proposed\n    regression tests before trusting them) generalizes and should be\n    considered for the rest of this repo's surface area, not treated as\n    GTG-specific tooling")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "kotoba-lang-standard-model"), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607051500" "adr-2607103000" "adr-2607103600")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607105000-kotoba-lang-standard-model-hypercharge-generator-bug-fix"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-10"), (:adr/body "see 2607105000-kotoba-lang-standard-model-hypercharge-generator-bug-fix.edn"), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/date "2026-07-10"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607105000: kotoba-lang/standard-model — extending independent-review discipline to the original 6 namespaces finds and fixes a real hypercharge-normalization bug"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))